---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Development Workflow — Varve Docs"
  description="How Varve preserves work, validates exact Git trees, certifies integration, and publishes releases with honest evidence."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <article class="workflow-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/docs')}>Documentation</a> / Development Workflow
      </nav>

      <header class="workflow-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">For contributors and maintainers</p>
        <h1>Evidence that follows the work</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Varve keeps development feedback fast while making integration and release decisions
          traceable. Every stage has a clear owner, an exact source identity, and an honest status.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="workflow-card workflow-card--accent" aria-labelledby="path-heading">
        <p class="workflow-kicker">The path</p>
        <h2 id="path-heading">Commit locally. Certify remotely. Publish deliberately.</h2>
        <div class="path-grid">
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="path-number">01</span>
            <h3>Shape the change</h3>
            <p>Keep commits focused and preserve unrelated work in the checkout.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="path-number">02</span>
            <h3>Check the impact</h3>
            <p>The planner selects the narrowest useful local and remote lanes.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="path-step">
            <span class="path-number">03</span>
            <h3>Freeze the source</h3>
            <p>CI, candidate checks, and Pages deployments carry the exact commit they ran.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="workflow-section" aria-labelledby="commands-heading">
        <p class="workflow-kicker">A practical start</p>
        <h2 id="commands-heading">Run the smallest useful check first</h2>
        <p>
          From the repository root, inspect the plan before starting a broader gate. The full
          suite is reserved for changes whose risk or release stage actually requires it.
        </p>
        <pre><code>pnpm verify:plan
pnpm verify:affected
pnpm verify:push</code></pre>
        <p>
          For a read-only view of synchronization and prior attempts, use
          <code>pnpm workflow:status</code>, <code>pnpm workflow:doctor</code>, and
          <code>pnpm workflow:history -- --json</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="workflow-section" aria-labelledby="honesty-heading">
        <p class="workflow-kicker">What the checks prove</p>
        <h2 id="honesty-heading">A green local hook is not a published release</h2>
        <div class="honesty-grid">
          <div>
            <h3>Local checkpoint</h3>
            <p>
              Git supplies the refs being pushed. Local lanes run against clean snapshots of those
              committed trees, while expensive browser, native, visual, and release work remains
              visible as CI responsibility.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Integration certification</h3>
            <p>
              The stable CI check reconciles selected jobs and deliberate skips against one exact
              commit. Missing, cancelled, timed-out, or unexpectedly skipped work is incomplete.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Release candidate</h3>
            <p>
              Triage can collect bounded failures without certifying anything. Only final mode can
              produce passed candidate evidence for the exact source and policy hash.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside class="workflow-note">
        <strong>Contributions are currently paused.</strong>
        <span>
          Bug reports, workflow proposals, documentation corrections, and cross-platform testing
          are welcome through the <a href={sitePath('/contribute')}>contribution guide</a>.
        </span>
      </aside>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .workflow-page {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .workflow-hero {
    max-width: 700px;
    padding: 3rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .workflow-kicker {
    color: var(--text-link);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .workflow-hero h1 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-editorial);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 4.4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 0.98;
    margin: 0.8rem 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .lead,
  .workflow-section > p:not(.workflow-kicker),
  .path-step p,
  .honesty-grid p,
  .workflow-note {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 650px;
  }

  .workflow-card,
  .workflow-section,
  .workflow-note {
    border-radius: var(--website-radius-card);
  }

  .workflow-card {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .workflow-card--accent {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    box-shadow: 0 1.5rem 4rem rgb(15 23 42 / 0.08);
  }

  .workflow-card h2,
  .workflow-section h2 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin: 0.55rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .path-grid,
  .honesty-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .path-step {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border-default);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  .path-number {
    color: var(--text-link);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .path-step h3,
  .honesty-grid h3 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0.35rem;
  }

  .path-step p,
  .honesty-grid p {
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .workflow-section {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .workflow-section > p:not(.workflow-kicker) {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  pre {
    background: var(--surface-code);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-code);
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .honesty-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .honesty-grid > div {
    background: var(--surface-muted);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .workflow-note {
    align-items: baseline;
    background: var(--surface-muted);
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .workflow-note strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .workflow-note a {
    color: var(--text-link);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .path-grid,
    .honesty-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .workflow-note {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .workflow-note strong {
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }
</style>
